From 544552959966f4c411672b4df54818c4b30971f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:36:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Analyzer: report suspected self-modifying stores, never
 patch them

The analyzer replaced every "store into an executable section, then j/jal"
with a NOP in the generated config. The README says self-modifying code is
"flagged but requires manual review"; now it is: the store is printed and
listed as a commented-out patch line in the TOML, and nothing is replaced.

A NOP doesn't make real self-modifying code work (the recompiled code still
runs the old instruction), and many PS2 ELFs have a single executable section
over code and data, so most hits are ordinary writes to globals. In Resident
Evil Outbreak (SLPM-65428) all 37 hits were data writes; 34 took effect, and
one left a CRI transfer buffer NULL, hanging the boot.

detectInstructionPatchesForHeuristics() runs the detection on given functions
and sections, for tests.
